## Objective

Build a small Notification System demonstrating inheritance, `extends`, `super`, constructor forwarding, method overriding, `@override`, polymorphism, collections of parent types, and type checking.

### Base Class
```dart
class AppNotification {
  final String message;

  AppNotification(this.message);

  void send() {
    print('Sending notification: $message');
  }
}
```

### Email Notification
```dart
class EmailNotification extends AppNotification {
  EmailNotification(super.message);

  @override
  void send() {
    print('Sending email: $message');
  }
}
```

### Push Notification
```dart
class PushNotification extends AppNotification {
  PushNotification(super.message);

  @override
  void send() {
    print('Sending push notification: $message');
  }
}
```

### Process Notifications
```dart
void processNotifications(
  List<AppNotification> notifications,
) {
  for (final notification in notifications) {
    notification.send();
  }
}
```

### Run
```dart
void main() {
  final notifications = <AppNotification>[
    EmailNotification('Your order has been confirmed.'),
    PushNotification('Your order is being prepared.'),
    EmailNotification('Your order has been shipped.'),
  ];

  processNotifications(notifications);
}
```

### Implementation Challenge
Add an `SMSNotification` class that extends `AppNotification` and overrides `send()`. The existing `processNotifications()` function should not need to change.

### Additional Inheritance Exercise
Create the following hierarchy:

```text
Animal
├── Dog
└── Cat
```

Then create:

```text
Animal
  ↓
Mammal
  ↓
Dog
```

The objective is to demonstrate hierarchical and multilevel inheritance separately.
